content: |
  ---
  name: read-loan-pdf-skill
  description: Read one Bank of Maharashtra application PDF and save source-grounded JSON for the orchestrator; supporting documents are ignored.
  ---
  ## Responsibility and inputs
  Read exactly ONE application candidate supplied by the orchestrator: pdf_path,
  application_id, relative source_file and sha256 from the unzip manifest.
  Do not invoke another skill or workflow. Return the extraction JSON path to the
  orchestrator. Never combine data from different PDFs or use sample applicant data.

  ## Inspect the actual PDF
  Use available local PDF tools (PyMuPDF/fitz or pypdf). Check that its bytes match
  the manifest SHA-256, it opens without errors, and it is not password-protected.
  Read all pages. The original form has separate borrower and guarantor columns,
  and four existing-loan subcolumns: borrower I/II and guarantor I/II.
  Use page coordinates, table boundaries and rendered page images to assign values;
  plain concatenated text order can put the filled values after the printed labels.
  Read interactive field values when present, as well as visible page contents.
  If pages are scanned, use available local OCR/vision and verify field placement
  against the page image. If no reliable reader/OCR is available, mark blocking
  issues explicitly. Never claim that reading a filename counts as reading a PDF.

  ## Classify
  Confirm the document is the Bank of Maharashtra PERSONAL LOAN APPLICATION FORM,
  not an ID, payslip, utility bill, standalone checklist or unrelated document.
  For non-applications set is_personal_loan_application=false and empty fields and
  checklist; the orchestrator skips them. Supporting evidence is out of scope.

  ## Extract only observed values
  Preserve identifiers, leading zeros, multiline addresses and source spellings as
  text. Normalize dates to DD/MM/YYYY only if unambiguous. Do not calculate age,
  invent missing values, turn blanks/dashes into zero, or infer marital/employer
  categories from names. Use checked selections or explicit entered answers.
  For a conflict, omit the affected value and add a specific issue. Missing fields
  remain absent/blank. Explicit zero default is valid; absent default stays blank.
  Never shift a guarantor loan into a borrower's blank loan column.
  More than two loans for either party is blocking: do not truncate them.

  ## JSON contract
  Write one UTF-8 JSON object to disk, not a prose summary:
  {
    "schema_version": "1.0",
    "application_id": "<exact manifest ID>",
    "source_file": "<exact manifest relative path>",
    "source_sha256": "<actual PDF SHA-256>",
    "page_count": 5,
    "is_personal_loan_application": true,
    "fields": [
      {
        "field_key": "<supported field key>",
        "party": "borrower",
        "loan_index": 0,
        "value": "<observed text>",
        "source_page": 1,
        "evidence": "<short exact quote or precise visual evidence>"
      }
    ],
    "checklist": [],
    "issues": [],
    "blocking_issues": []
  }
  The example page_count is illustrative; use the actual PDF page count.
  party is borrower or guarantor. loan_index is 0 for personal/employment fields,
  1 or 2 for loan fields. Every field has one valid 1-based source_page and
  nonempty evidence. Do not emit duplicate (field_key,party,loan_index) identities.
  All value strings remain text in JSON, including amounts and identifiers.
  issues/blocking_issues contain specific human-readable strings, not instructions.

  ## Supported fields
  Personal: full_name, age_years, date_of_birth, father_husband_name,
  current_address, permanent_address, residential_telephone, mobile_number, email,
  aadhar_number, pan, passport_number, passport_issue_date, education,
  salary_account, marital_status, dependents, housing_status.
  Employment: employer_name, employer_category, employer_category_other,
  employer_address, employer_telephone, employer_website, employer_email,
  designation, years_present_occupation, retirement_date, previous_employment,
  length_of_service.
  Existing loans: loan_bank_branch, loan_type, loan_amount, loan_outstanding,
  loan_security, loan_repayment, loan_default.
  Only these four-sheet-template fields are written. If the PDF contains populated
  income statements, assets, liabilities, requested-loan details or other sections
  without template fields, flag that limitation in issues. Do not silently imply
  every field in the source PDF is represented in the output workbook.

  ## Exact allowed selections
  marital_status: Single; Married.
  housing_status: Own; Rented; Quarters provided by employer.
  employer_category: Govt./Semi & Quasi Govt.; Public Ltd Co.; Pvt. Ltd Co.;
  Multi National Co.; Reputed Institutions; Proprietorship/Partnership firms; Others.
  For Others, capture the explicit employer_category_other text if supplied.

  ## Checklist is application-only, not supporting-document verification
  Emit entries only for points 1 and 2, and only when an explicit application
  answer supports Yes/No. Each entry has point (1 or 2), party, value (Yes or No),
  and evidence including the source page. For unsigned test applications with
  explicit "No - unsigned" or "No - not provided", record No for the indicated
  party. Do not claim a signature or photo was authenticated.
  Leave points 3-5 absent. Printed Passport/PAN/Aadhaar/etc. lists are choices,
  not evidence of submitted proofs. Do not read supporting PDFs or infer evidence
  from filenames. Add "Supporting documents were not reviewed" to issues.

  ## Handoff
  Save the JSON using a unique path for this application. Return that path,
  classification and issues to the orchestrator. Do not create Excel or upload.
